                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Likes:\n\n+ Enormous amounts of gear to unlock (weapons, shields, axes, trinkets, potions, scrolls... it goes on!), all of which can be enhanced via card drops earned from gameplay\n+ Simple gameplay loop makes this game easy to jump in and play a few rounds during a break\n+ Hero-defense (like a moving tower) gameplay requiring active resource management, positioning, and encourages experimenting with different loadouts\n+ At the time of this review I'm just over half way done the campaign and I've clocked nearly 15hrs\n+ Two characters to choose from, each with their own set of skills/spells, helps provide some variety\n+ No F2P microtransactions, all of which have been removed and re-balanced for the PC release\n+ Decent variety of enemy types, towers, and bosses\n+ Steady stream of unlockables, you're always earning something!\n+ Light RPG mechanics like a upgradeable talents, spells, and skills.\n+ Comic book style artwork\n+ Animations are fluid\n\n\nDislikes:\n\n- UI is very \"mobile\" and lacks some PC-specific features, like hovering over items to see stats (on mobile you have to tap them)\n- The gameplay loop can become very repetitive for some players\n- Requires an online connection... for some reason.\n\n\nOverall, it's a fun game for what it sets out to be. If you're a fan of tower/hero defense games, then it may be worth giving Bravium a shot.\n\nIf you're interested in seeing more gameplay, I've started a Let's Play series: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLwIDRHkaAZ21wtLj7Ux-CWkgU2DhZoc7t",
